  "operative_text": "Section 1 (N.D.C.C. 62.1-01-01(5)): \"Government building\" means a building or a portion of a building which is owned, possessed, or used by or leased to the state of North Dakota, or any of its political subdivisions and in which access is not permitted unless an individual passes through equipment that detects weapons and is staffed by armed security personnel.\nSection 2 (N.D.C.C. 62.1-02-05(1)): An individual who knowingly possesses a firearm or dangerous weapon at a public gathering is guilty of a class B misdemeanor."
}